<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese treasury bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese treasury bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its November 7 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		    Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  14.05 (14.10)	     14.56  (14.61)</p>
<p>    Six months	    15.58 (15.60)	     16.89  (16.92)</p>
<p>    12 months	     15.08 (15.10)	     17.75  (17.78)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 21.58  (21.62)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
